  "name": "apigee-agent-gateway-governance",
  "description": "Stands up an Apigee API proxy that a Google Cloud Agent Gateway calls as an ext-proc (Service Extension) callout on an agent's LLM traffic, to meter token usage per model, extract caller identity, and apply Model Armor prompt screening or a semantic cache. Use when wiring Apigee in as an AI gateway behind an Agent Gateway, when an agent's model egress needs governing, or when a callout proxy returns no verdict and you need to find out why. The distinguishing question is whether Apigee forwards the traffic or only inspects it: this skill is inspect-only, and builds the proxy itself. Don't use it when Apigee is meant to receive a request and route it onward to a backend — including hosting an MCP server behind Apigee — which needs a proxy with a target instead. Don't use for governing the agent's calls to tools or MCP servers. Don't use for choosing or switching which model a request goes to. Don't use for creating the Agent Gateway itself, nor for Apigee hybrid.",
  "stars": 22796,
